I'll cut it with the scissors.

274
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:18,740
And I can do the sewing.

275
00:19:18,830 --> 00:19:20,870
Leave the sewing to the women.

276
00:19:20,950 --> 00:19:22,450
You go get some trimmin'.

277
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:26,460
And we'll make
a lovely dress for Cinderelly, whoo

278
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:29,300
We'll make a lovely dress
for Cinderelly

279
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:31,670
Follow me, Gus-Gus.
I know where to go.

280
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:34,170
It's gonna be pretty, this dress.

281
00:19:35,430 --> 00:19:37,140
Cinderelly will be surprised.

282
00:19:37,220 --> 00:19:39,470
Surprised, surprised. Very surprised.

283
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:50,520
And this, too, my slippers.
Don't forget...

284
00:19:50,610 --> 00:19:52,980
- Take my dress.
- Here, mend the buttonholes.

285
00:19:53,070 --> 00:19:56,400
- Press my skirt and mind the ruffle.
- Cinderella?

286
00:19:56,490 --> 00:19:58,280
- Yes?
- When you're through,

287
00:19:58,370 --> 00:20:01,160
and before you begin
your regular chores,

288
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:02,990
I have a few little things.

289
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:04,330
Very well.

290
00:20:04,410 --> 00:20:07,830
I don't see why everyone else
has nice things to wear,

291
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:10,000
and I always end up in these old rags.

292
00:20:10,090 --> 00:20:13,010
This sash! I wouldn't be seen dead in it.

293
00:20:13,090 --> 00:20:15,340
You should talk. These beads!

294
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:16,760
I am sick of looking at them.

295
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:19,470
- Trash.
- Oh, I hate this.

296
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:25,180
Come on and be careful.

297
00:20:25,270 --> 00:20:28,600
Yes, yes, yes. Real careful.

298
00:20:38,620 --> 00:20:40,570
We can use that, Gus-Gus.

299
00:20:40,950 --> 00:20:42,700
Pretty, pretty.

300
00:20:42,790 --> 00:20:44,990
Look out. Lucify!

301
00:21:31,630 --> 00:21:33,420
Beads!

302
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:35,960
Very pretty beads!

303
00:23:40,090 --> 00:23:43,710
A dream is a wish your heart makes

304
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:47,720
When you're fast asleep

305
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:49,390
In dreams you will lose
your heartaches

306
00:23:49,390 --> 00:23:50,720
Oh, well.

307
00:23:50,810 --> 00:23:52,640
What's a royal ball?

308
00:23:54,560 --> 00:23:57,650
After all, I suppose
it would be frightfully dull,

309
00:23:57,730 --> 00:24:01,230
and boring, and completely...

310
00:24:01,980 --> 00:24:03,940
Completely wonderful.

311
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:14,120
- It's my...
- Surprise!

312
00:24:14,210 --> 00:24:16,040
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

313
00:24:17,460 --> 00:24:19,590
- Happy birthday!
- No, no, no, no!

314
00:24:19,670 --> 00:24:22,090
Well, I never dreamed it.

315
00:24:22,170 --> 00:24:24,760
It's such a surprise.

316
00:24:25,010 --> 00:24:28,340
Oh, how can I ever...

317
00:24:29,050 --> 00:24:31,470
Oh, thank you so much.

318
00:24:38,520 --> 00:24:41,110
Remember, when you're
presented to His Highness,

319
00:24:41,190 --> 00:24:42,860
- be sure...
- Wait!

320
00:24:43,860 --> 00:24:45,650
Please, wait for me.

321
00:24:46,530 --> 00:24:49,370
Isn't it lovely? Do you like it?

322
00:24:49,370 --> 00:24:50,200
- Oh, but I'm not...
- Of course, you are.

323
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:51,660
But we have to hurry,

324
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:53,990
because even miracles take a little time.

325
00:24:54,080 --> 00:24:57,580
- Miracles?
- Watch.

326
00:24:57,670 --> 00:25:00,630
What in the world did I do
with that magic wand? I was sure...

327
00:25:00,710 --> 00:25:01,880
Magic wand?

328
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:03,550
That's strange.

329
00:25:03,630 --> 00:25:06,340
- I always...
- Then you must be...

330
00:25:06,420 --> 00:25:09,550
Your fairy godmother? Of course.

331
00:25:09,640 --> 00:25:12,010
Where is that wand? I...

332
00:25:12,680 --> 00:25:14,680
Oh! I forgot.

333
00:25:14,770 --> 00:25:16,270
I put it away.

334
00:25:18,940 --> 00:25:20,480
Look at what she did.

335
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:22,020
How'd she do it?

336
00:25:22,110 --> 00:25:25,150
Now, let's see.

337
00:25:25,230 --> 00:25:28,400
I'd say the first thing you need is

338
00:25:28,490 --> 00:25:30,820
- a pumpkin.
- A pumpkin?

339
00:25:30,910 --> 00:25:34,450
Now the magic words.

340
00:25:39,460 --> 00:25:44,380
Sala-gadoola-menchika-boo-la
Bibbidi-bobbidi-boo

341
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:46,550
Put 'em together
and what have you got?

342
00:25:46,630 --> 00:25:48,670
Bibbidi-bobbidi-boo

343
00:25:48,760 --> 00:25:53,220
Sala-gadoola-menchika-boo-la
Bibbidi-bobbidi-boo

344
00:25:53,310 --> 00:25:55,560
It'll do magic
Believe it or not

345
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:57,720
Bibbidi-bobbidi-boo

346
00:25:57,810 --> 00:26:02,230
Now sala-gadoola means
Menchika-boolaroo

347
00:26:02,310 --> 00:26:04,730
But the thing-a-ma-bob
that does the job

348
00:26:04,820 --> 00:26:07,440
Is bibbidi-bobbidi-boo

349
00:26:07,530 --> 00:26:12,070
Sala-gadoola-menchika-boo-la
Bibbidi-bobbidi-boo

350
00:26:12,160 --> 00:26:14,240
Put 'em together
and what have you got?

351
00:26:14,330 --> 00:26:18,200
Bibbidi-bobbidi
Bibbidi-bobbidi Bibbidi-bobbidi-boo

352
00:26:19,660 --> 00:26:20,960
Oh, looky.

353
00:26:21,040 --> 00:26:22,830
Isn't it wonderful?

354
00:26:23,670 --> 00:26:25,960
Oh, it's beautiful.

355
00:26:26,050 --> 00:26:28,460
Yes, isn't it?

356
00:26:28,550 --> 00:26:30,970
With an elegant coach like that,
of course,

357
00:26:31,050 --> 00:26:33,840
we'll simply have to have

358
00:26:34,180 --> 00:26:36,720
- mice!
- Mice?

359
00:26:36,810 --> 00:26:39,270
Oh, this really is nice.

360
00:26:39,350 --> 00:26:42,440
Why, we'll have a coach
and four when we're through.

361
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:45,980
Just a wave of my stick
and to finish the trick,

362
00:26:46,070 --> 00:26:48,980
bibbidi, bobbidi, boo.

363
00:26:49,070 --> 00:26:51,110
Gracious, what did I do?

364
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:54,990
I was sure there were four.
There should be one more.

365
00:26:55,080 --> 00:26:57,080
There you are.

366
00:26:58,450 --> 00:27:00,580
Bibbidi, bobbidi, boo.

367
00:27:10,880 --> 00:27:13,090
Oh, poor Lucifer.

368
00:27:13,180 --> 00:27:15,470
Serves him right, I'd say. Now...

369
00:27:15,550 --> 00:27:18,470
Where were we? Oh, goodness, yes.

370
00:27:18,560 --> 00:27:21,100
You can't go to the ball without

371
00:27:21,180 --> 00:27:22,640
a horse.

372
00:27:22,730 --> 00:27:24,230
Another one?

373
00:27:24,730 --> 00:27:28,400
But tonight, for a change,
you will handle the reins,

374
00:27:28,480 --> 00:27:30,900
and sit in the driver's seat, too.

375
00:27:31,360 --> 00:27:34,950
For instead of a horse,
you're the coachman, of course.

376
00:27:35,030 --> 00:27:36,950
Bibbidi, bobbidi, boo.

377
00:27:41,040 --> 00:27:44,500
That does it, I guess, except for...
Oh, yes!

378
00:27:44,580 --> 00:27:47,710
The finishing touch. And, that's you.

379
00:27:47,790 --> 00:27:51,590
Yes, Bruno, that's right,
you'll be footman tonight.

380
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:54,260
Bibbidi, bobbidi, boo.

381
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:58,260
Well, well, hop in, my dear.
We can't waste time.

382
00:27:58,350 --> 00:28:01,060
- But...
- No, don't try to thank me.

383
00:28:01,140 --> 00:28:04,810
Oh, I wasn't... I mean, I do, but...

384
00:28:04,890 --> 00:28:06,560
But, don't you think my dress...

385
00:28:06,650 --> 00:28:09,480
Yes, it's lovely, dear.

386
00:28:09,570 --> 00:28:13,480
Good heavens, child.
You can't go in that!

387
00:28:15,110 --> 00:28:17,360
Now, let's see, dear.

388
00:28:17,450 --> 00:28:21,700
Your size and the shade of your eyes.

389
00:28:21,790 --> 00:28:24,910
Something simple, but daring, too.

390
00:28:24,100 --> 00:28:28,750
Oh, just leave it to me.
What a gown this will be.

391
00:28:29,210 --> 00:28:31,460
Bibbidi-bobbidi.
Bibbidi-bobbidi.

392
00:28:31,550 --> 00:28:33,880
Bibbidi-bobbidi-boo.

393
00:28:36,130 --> 00:28:39,340
Oh, it's a beautiful dress.

394
00:28:39,430 --> 00:28:42,640
Did you ever see
such a beautiful dress?

395
00:28:42,720 --> 00:28:45,480
And, look, glass slippers.

396
00:28:47,230 --> 00:28:49,400
Why, it's like a dream.

397
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:52,400
A wonderful dream come true.

398
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:54,070
Yes, my child.

399
00:28:54,150 --> 00:28:55,820
But, like all dreams,

400
00:28:55,900 --> 00:28:58,700
well, I'm afraid this can't last forever.

401
00:28:58,780 --> 00:29:00,820
You'll have only till midnight, and then...

402
00:29:00,910 --> 00:29:02,490
Midnight? Thank you.

403
00:29:02,580 --> 00:29:05,950
Now, now, now, just a minute.
You must understand, my dear,

404
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:09,250
on the stroke of 12:00
the spell will be broken,

405
00:29:09,330 --> 00:29:11,920
and everything will be as it was before.

406
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,250
Oh, I understand, but

407
00:29:14,340 --> 00:29:17,010
it's more than I ever hoped for.

408
00:29:17,090 --> 00:29:18,800
Bless you, my child.

409
00:29:18,880 --> 00:29:21,390
I... Goodness me!

410
00:29:21,470 --> 00:29:24,720
It's getting late.
Hurry up, dear. The ball can't wait.

411
00:29:24,850 --> 00:29:27,140
Have a good time.
Dance, be gay.

412
00:29:27,230 --> 00:29:29,390
Now, off you go.
You're on your way.

413
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:31,770
With a bibbidi-bobbidi
Bibbidi-bobbidi

414
00:29:31,860 --> 00:29:33,520
Bibbidi-bobbidi-boo

415
00:30:01,430 --> 00:30:05,180
Princess Frederica
Eugenie de la Fontain.

416
00:30:09,560 --> 00:30:12,350
Mademoiselle
Augustina DuBois.

417
00:30:12,440 --> 00:30:15,860
Daughter of General Pierre DuBois.

418
00:30:26,410 --> 00:30:29,250
The boy isn't cooperating.

419
00:30:30,080 --> 00:30:34,210
Mademoiselle Leonora
Mercedes de la Tour.

420
00:30:34,290 --> 00:30:38,710
Daughter of Colonel
and Madame de la Tour.

421
00:30:45,260 --> 00:30:47,760
I can't understand it.

422
00:30:47,850 --> 00:30:50,890
There must be at least one
who'd make a suitable mother.

423
00:30:50,980 --> 00:30:52,850
Sire.

424
00:30:52,940 --> 00:30:55,400
A suitable wife.

425
00:31:14,500 --> 00:31:20,050
Mademoiselles
Drizella and Anastasia Tremaine.

426
00:31:20,130 --> 00:31:22,800
Daughters of Lady Tremaine.

427
00:31:29,100 --> 00:31:32,600
I give up.
Even I couldn't expect the boy to...

428
00:31:32,680 --> 00:31:36,230
Well, if I may say so,
Your Majesty, I did try to warn you,

429
00:31:36,310 --> 00:31:40,150
but you, Sire, are incurably romantic.

430
00:31:40,610 --> 00:31:45,200
No doubt you saw
the whole pretty picture in detail.

431
00:31:45,820 --> 00:31:49,620
The young Prince
bowing to the assembly.

432
00:31:50,410 --> 00:31:53,500
Suddenly he stops. He looks up.

433
00:31:53,580 --> 00:31:57,120
For, lo, there she stands.

434
00:31:57,630 --> 00:31:59,500
The girl of his dreams.

435
00:32:01,260 --> 00:32:03,170
Who she is or whence she came,

436
00:32:03,760 --> 00:32:06,090
he knows not, nor does he care,

437
00:32:06,180 --> 00:32:08,970
for his heart tells him that here,

438
00:32:09,060 --> 00:32:14,100
here is the maid
predestined to be his bride.

439
00:32:15,940 --> 00:32:18,610
A pretty plot for fairy tales, Sire.

440
00:32:18,690 --> 00:32:20,820
But in real life, oh, no.

441
00:32:20,900 --> 00:32:24,190
No! It was foredoomed to failure.

442
00:32:24,530 --> 00:32:27,070
Failure, eh?

443
00:32:27,160 --> 00:32:30,330
Take a look at that,
you pompous windbag.

444
00:32:31,620 --> 00:32:32,950
Who is she?

445
00:32:33,040 --> 00:32:35,120
- You know her?
- No, Sire.

446
00:32:35,210 --> 00:32:37,290
I've never seen her before.

447
00:32:37,380 --> 00:32:39,670
That's one thing in her favour.

448
00:32:39,750 --> 00:32:41,710
The waltz. Quick, the waltz!

449
00:32:45,510 --> 00:32:48,590
Lights. The lights.

450
00:33:07,570 --> 00:33:09,990
Failure, eh?

451
00:33:13,870 --> 00:33:17,330
Well... Now for a good night's sleep.

452
00:33:17,410 --> 00:33:20,120
Oh, quite so, Sire. I believe I, too...

453
00:33:20,210 --> 00:33:22,960
You will stay right here.

454
00:33:23,050 --> 00:33:26,670
See they're not disturbed,
and when the boy proposes,

455
00:33:26,760 --> 00:33:29,840
notify me immediately.

456
00:33:29,930 --> 00:33:31,390
Notify me immediately.

457
00:33:31,470 --> 00:33:33,180
And remember,

458
00:33:33,260 --> 00:33:35,770
if anything goes wrong...

459
00:33:52,080 --> 00:33:54,660
- Who is she, Mother?
- Do we know her?

460
00:33:54,740 --> 00:33:57,200
Well, the Prince certainly seems to.

461
00:33:57,290 --> 00:33:59,370
I know I've never seen her.

462
00:33:59,460 --> 00:34:00,790
Nor I.

463
00:34:00,880 --> 00:34:03,880
But she certainly is... Wait.

464
00:34:04,630 --> 00:34:07,210
There is something familiar about her.

465
00:34:17,640 --> 00:34:18,720
Ahem.

466
00:34:28,240 --> 00:34:37,240
So this is love

467
00:34:37,330 --> 00:34:41,250
So this is what makes life

468
00:34:41,330 --> 00:34:44,460
Divine

469
00:34:44,540 --> 00:34:48,050
I'm all aglow

470
00:34:48,130 --> 00:34:52,470
- And now I know
- And now I know

471
00:34:52,550 --> 00:34:57,050
The key to all Heaven

472
00:34:57,140 --> 00:35:00,600
Is mine

473
00:35:00,680 --> 00:35:04,690
My heart has wings

474
00:35:04,770 --> 00:35:08,780
And I can fly

475
00:35:08,860 --> 00:35:12,700
I'll touch every star

476
00:35:12,780 --> 00:35:16,030
In the sky

477
00:35:17,280 --> 00:35:22,160
So this is the miracle

478
00:35:22,250 --> 00:35:28,040
That I've been dreaming of

479
00:35:37,100 --> 00:35:39,510
So this

480
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:42,220
Is

481
00:35:42,310 --> 00:35:45,730
Love

482
00:35:49,150 --> 00:35:50,730
Oh. Oh, my goodness.

483
00:35:50,820 --> 00:35:52,570
What's the matter?

484
00:35:52,650 --> 00:35:53,900
It's midnight.

485
00:35:53,990 --> 00:35:55,990
Yes, so it is. But why...

486
00:35:56,070 --> 00:35:58,370
- Goodbye.
- No, no, wait.

487
00:35:58,450 --> 00:36:01,160
- You can't go now. It's only...
- Oh, I must. Please.

488
00:36:01,240 --> 00:36:02,870
- Please, I must.
- But why?

489
00:36:02,950 --> 00:36:05,210
Well, I... Oh, the Prince,

490
00:36:05,290 --> 00:36:06,750
I haven't met the Prince.

491
00:36:06,830 --> 00:36:08,170
The Prince?

492
00:36:08,250 --> 00:36:09,380
But didn't you know...

493
00:36:10,670 --> 00:36:12,840
- Goodbye.
- No, wait.

494
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:15,220
Come back. Please come back.

495
00:36:15,550 --> 00:36:18,140
I don't even know your name.
How will I find you?

496
00:36:18,220 --> 00:36:19,760
Wait! Please wait.

497
00:36:20,890 --> 00:36:22,220
Goodbye.

498
00:36:22,810 --> 00:36:25,060
Oh, I say. Young lady.

499
00:36:25,140 --> 00:36:28,360
- Wait!
- The Prince!

500
00:36:53,630 --> 00:36:55,090
I'm sorry.

501
00:36:55,840 --> 00:36:59,090
I guess I forgot about everything.

502
00:37:00,050 --> 00:37:01,850
Even the time, but...

503
00:37:03,310 --> 00:37:06,060
But it was so wonderful.

504
00:37:07,100 --> 00:37:09,020
And he was so handsome,

505
00:37:09,110 --> 00:37:11,520
and when we danced...

506
00:37:11,610 --> 00:37:15,240
Oh, I'm sure even the Prince
himself couldn't have been more...

507
00:37:15,320 --> 00:37:16,530
More...

508
00:37:17,700 --> 00:37:20,360
- Oh, well, it's over and...
- Cinderelly.

509
00:37:20,450 --> 00:37:22,450
Look, look! The slippers!

510
00:37:22,580 --> 00:37:23,660
Yeah, your slipper.

511
00:37:23,740 --> 00:37:25,950
Your slipper, Cinderelly.

512
00:37:30,080 --> 00:37:31,420
Thank you.

513
00:37:32,130 --> 00:37:35,050
Thank you so much, for everything.

514
00:37:44,890 --> 00:37:49,270
Your Majesty,
I see no point in beating about the bush.

515
00:37:49,350 --> 00:37:51,310
I regret to inform you, Sire,

516
00:37:51,400 --> 00:37:53,570
