518
00:37:56,530 --> 00:37:58,320
Yes. I'll do it.

519
00:38:00,490 --> 00:38:03,660
No. I just can't.

520
00:38:32,310 --> 00:38:33,980
Well, come in.

521
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:36,110
Come in!

522
00:38:36,190 --> 00:38:39,400
- Your Majesty...
- So, he's proposed already?

523
00:38:39,490 --> 00:38:40,950
- Tell me about it.
- Well...

524
00:38:41,030 --> 00:38:43,450
- Who is she?
- I didn't get a chance...

525
00:38:43,530 --> 00:38:46,160
No matter. We've more
important things to discuss.

526
00:38:46,240 --> 00:38:47,910
Arrangements for the wedding,

527
00:38:47,990 --> 00:38:50,620
invitations, a national holiday.

528
00:38:51,330 --> 00:38:53,580
- All that sort of thing.
- But, Sire...

529
00:38:53,670 --> 00:38:56,340
Here. Have a cigar. Take a few more.

530
00:38:56,880 --> 00:38:57,920
But...

531
00:38:58,010 --> 00:39:00,800
Better practise passing these out, eh?

532
00:39:00,880 --> 00:39:04,140
But, if you'd only listen.

533
00:39:04,220 --> 00:39:05,970
And for you, my friend.

534
00:39:06,050 --> 00:39:09,810
- Your Majesty, please...
- A knighthood.

535
00:39:09,890 --> 00:39:12,390
I hereby dub you Sir...

536
00:39:13,690 --> 00:39:16,270
By the way, what title would you like?

537
00:39:16,770 --> 00:39:19,820
- Sire? She got away.
- Sir "She Got Away"?

538
00:39:19,900 --> 00:39:22,070
A peculiar title, but if that's what you...

539
00:39:22,990 --> 00:39:25,740
She what? Why, you...

540
00:39:25,870 --> 00:39:27,990
You... You traitor!

541
00:39:28,080 --> 00:39:30,990
Now, Sire.
Remember, your blood pressure.

542
00:39:31,080 --> 00:39:32,960
Treason!

543
00:39:35,790 --> 00:39:37,340
No, Sire. No!

544
00:39:37,420 --> 00:39:39,800
Sabotage!

545
00:39:40,760 --> 00:39:42,670
You were in league with the Prince.

546
00:39:42,760 --> 00:39:44,800
I tried to stop her,

547
00:39:44,890 --> 00:39:46,760
but she vanished into thin air.

548
00:39:46,840 --> 00:39:48,600
A likely story.

549
00:39:48,680 --> 00:39:52,020
But it's true, Sire.
All we could find was this glass slipper.

550
00:39:52,100 --> 00:39:54,600
The whole thing was a plot!

551
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:58,190
But, Sire, he loves her.

552
00:39:58,270 --> 00:40:00,190
He won't rest till he finds her.

553
00:40:00,280 --> 00:40:02,190
He's determined to marry her.

554
00:40:03,570 --> 00:40:06,530
What? What did you say?

555
00:40:06,910 --> 00:40:09,490
The Prince, Sire,
swears he'll marry none

556
00:40:09,580 --> 00:40:11,700
but the girl who fits this slipper.

557
00:40:11,790 --> 00:40:13,580
He said that, did he?

558
00:40:14,620 --> 00:40:17,210
We've got him!

559
00:40:22,300 --> 00:40:25,720
But, Sire, this slipper
may fit one of any number of girls.

560
00:40:25,800 --> 00:40:28,680
That's his problem. He's given his word.

561
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:31,890
- We'll hold him to it.
- No, Your Highness.

562
00:40:31,970 --> 00:40:33,970
I'll have nothing to do with it.

563
00:40:34,060 --> 00:40:36,770
You'll try this
on every maid in my kingdom.

564
00:40:36,850 --> 00:40:38,100
And if the shoe fits,

565
00:40:39,690 --> 00:40:41,570
bring her in.

566
00:40:41,650 --> 00:40:44,440
Yes, Your Majesty.

567
00:40:58,330 --> 00:41:00,540
Cinderella? Cinderella?

568
00:41:01,420 --> 00:41:03,710
- Cinderella! Where is that...
- Yes?

569
00:41:03,800 --> 00:41:05,130
Here I am.

570
00:41:05,670 --> 00:41:07,090
My daughters, where are they?

571
00:41:07,180 --> 00:41:08,680
I think they're still in bed.

572
00:41:10,510 --> 00:41:14,180
Don't just stand there!
Bring up the breakfast trays at once.

573
00:41:14,270 --> 00:41:15,470
And hurry!

574
00:41:16,430 --> 00:41:18,690
Wow. I wonder what's the matter.

575
00:41:18,770 --> 00:41:20,480
What's the matter with her?

576
00:41:20,560 --> 00:41:22,770
I don't know. Let's find out. Come on.

577
00:41:30,660 --> 00:41:32,780
Drizella. Drizella!

578
00:41:32,870 --> 00:41:34,990
What?

579
00:41:35,080 --> 00:41:37,040
Get up. Quick. This instant.

580
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:38,100
We haven't a moment to lose.

581
00:41:40,210 --> 00:41:43,340
Anastasia.

582
00:41:46,090 --> 00:41:47,340
Get up, Anastasia.

583
00:41:48,470 --> 00:41:50,680
What for? Why?

584
00:41:50,760 --> 00:41:53,600
Everyone's talking about it,
the whole kingdom.

585
00:41:53,890 --> 00:41:56,180
- Hurry now. He'll be here any minute.
- Who will?

586
00:41:56,270 --> 00:41:59,310
The Grand Duke.
He's been hunting all night.

587
00:41:59,390 --> 00:42:01,480
- Hunting?
- For that girl.

588
00:42:01,560 --> 00:42:04,110
The one who lost
her slipper at the ball last night.

589
00:42:04,190 --> 00:42:06,150
They say he's madly in love with her.

590
00:42:06,240 --> 00:42:09,030
- The Duke is?
- No, no, no. The Prince!

591
00:42:09,030 --> 00:42:09,900
May we offer you some tea?

592
00:42:09,990 --> 00:42:12,570
What? Tea?

593
00:42:12,660 --> 00:42:14,950
Thank you, madam, no.

594
00:42:15,030 --> 00:42:17,620
We must proceed with the fitting.

595
00:42:17,700 --> 00:42:20,080
Of course. Anastasia, dear.

596
00:42:24,340 --> 00:42:27,130
There. I knew it was my slipper.

597
00:42:27,760 --> 00:42:29,260
Exactly my size.

598
00:42:29,340 --> 00:42:31,180
I always wear the same size.

599
00:42:31,340 --> 00:42:33,140
As soon as I saw it, I said...

600
00:42:33,220 --> 00:42:35,100
Oh, well...

601
00:42:35,180 --> 00:42:37,930
It may be a trifle snug today.

602
00:42:38,020 --> 00:42:40,600
You know how it is, dancing all night.

603
00:42:40,690 --> 00:42:42,560
I can't understand why.

604
00:42:42,650 --> 00:42:44,690
It's always fit perfectly before.

605
00:42:45,110 --> 00:42:46,980
I don't think you're half trying.

606
00:42:47,780 --> 00:42:50,110
Mother, can you...

607
00:42:50,200 --> 00:42:53,490
Quiet, my dear.
We mustn't disturb His Grace.

608
00:42:53,570 --> 00:42:57,120
Young man, are you sure
you're trying it on the right foot?

609
00:42:58,870 --> 00:43:02,620
Oh, it's the right foot, but...

610
00:43:02,710 --> 00:43:04,460
These glass shoes
aren't always reliable.

611
00:43:04,540 --> 00:43:06,460
Come on, hurry.

612
00:43:06,550 --> 00:43:08,420
Up the stairs, up the stairs!

613
00:43:10,050 --> 00:43:12,260
Lucify, Lucify.

614
00:43:15,640 --> 00:43:18,050
Up, up, up with it.

615
00:43:28,070 --> 00:43:29,230
Here.

616
00:43:45,250 --> 00:43:47,170
Why can't you hold still a minute?

617
00:43:47,250 --> 00:43:50,300
My word. Enough of this!

618
00:43:52,970 --> 00:43:55,010
The next young lady, please.

619
00:43:55,090 --> 00:43:56,720
Did you hear that, Gus?

620
00:43:56,800 --> 00:43:58,850
- Yup.
- Gotta hurry.

621
00:44:04,600 --> 00:44:06,600
Come on, come on, hurry.

622
00:44:14,150 --> 00:44:17,110
Gus-Gus, Gus-Gus, come on.

623
00:44:17,200 --> 00:44:20,030
Look, look. Just up there. Come on.

624
00:44:28,920 --> 00:44:31,090
Us is coming, Cinderelly.

625
00:44:31,170 --> 00:44:33,760
- I can get you out.
- You've got the key!

626
00:44:33,840 --> 00:44:36,760
How did you ever manage to...

627
00:44:36,840 --> 00:44:38,430
Lucifer!

628
00:44:38,510 --> 00:44:40,800
Let him go, Lucifer.

629
00:44:41,640 --> 00:44:43,430
Please, let him go.

630
00:44:44,060 --> 00:44:46,020
- Let him go.
- Let him go!

631
00:44:46,100 --> 00:44:48,560
Let him go. Let him out, you hear?

632
00:44:48,650 --> 00:44:50,400
Lucify, you...

633
00:45:28,520 --> 00:45:31,860
Bruno. Yes, Bruno!

634
00:45:32,270 --> 00:45:35,070
Quick, get Bruno. Get Bruno!

635
00:45:55,340 --> 00:45:58,550
Of all the stupid little idiots.

636
00:45:59,380 --> 00:46:01,220
I'll do it myself.

637
00:46:01,300 --> 00:46:03,010
Get away from me.

638
00:46:03,100 --> 00:46:06,140
I'll make it fit.

639
00:46:06,720 --> 00:46:08,560
- There.
- It fits.

640
00:46:08,640 --> 00:46:09,890
It fits?

641
00:46:12,060 --> 00:46:14,110
No!

642
00:46:20,160 --> 00:46:22,860
Oh, Your Grace, I'm dreadfully sorry.

643
00:46:23,240 --> 00:46:24,780
It shan't happen again.

644
00:46:24,870 --> 00:46:26,330
Precisely, madam.

645
00:46:52,600 --> 00:46:55,610
Come on, come on.
Get up, Gus-Gus, get up.

646
00:46:56,150 --> 00:46:58,110
Don't, don't, don't, don't.

647
00:46:58,780 --> 00:47:00,740
Let go, let go.

648
00:47:05,370 --> 00:47:08,450
You are the only ladies
in the household I hope... I presume.

649
00:47:08,540 --> 00:47:11,250
- There's no one else, Your Grace.
- Quite so.

650
00:47:11,330 --> 00:47:13,920
- Good day. Good day.
- Your Grace?

651
00:47:14,290 --> 00:47:17,040
Your Grace, please, wait.

652
00:47:17,130 --> 00:47:19,260
May I try it on?

653
00:47:19,340 --> 00:47:22,170
- Pay no attention.
- It's Cinderella.

654
00:47:22,260 --> 00:47:24,130
- From the kitchen.
- Ridiculous.

655
00:47:24,220 --> 00:47:26,260
She's out of her mind.

656
00:47:26,350 --> 00:47:28,260
Just an imaginative child.

657
00:47:28,350 --> 00:47:31,350
Madam,
my orders were "every maiden."

658
00:47:32,890 --> 00:47:34,440
Come, my child.

659
00:47:49,490 --> 00:47:51,370
Oh, no.

660
00:47:51,450 --> 00:47:53,910
No, no, no. Oh, no!

661
00:47:53,100 --> 00:47:56,040
Oh, this is terrible.

662
00:47:56,130 --> 00:47:58,340
The King, what will he say?

663
00:47:59,130 --> 00:48:00,590
What will he do?

664
00:48:00,670 --> 00:48:02,210
Perhaps, if it would help...

665
00:48:02,300 --> 00:48:05,720
No, no. Nothing can help now. Nothing.

666
00:48:05,840 --> 00:48:07,800
But, you see, I have the other slipper.

667
00:48:46,130 --> 00:48:48,890
Have faith in dreams

668
00:48:48,970 --> 00:48:51,680
And someday

669
00:48:51,760 --> 00:48:57,310
Your rainbow
will come smiling through

670
00:48:57,390 --> 00:49:02,190
No matter how your heart is grieving

671
00:49:02,280 --> 00:49:06,450
If you keep on believing

672
00:49:06,530 --> 00:49:09,780
The dream that you wish

673
00:49:09,870 --> 00:49:13,870
Will come true
